; The demos and the art they are built from: one small world per engine
; feature, plus the five-room showcase level that has all of them at once.
; Nothing in the engine depends on any of this, by design: it is content, and
; content lives outside the library it is content for.
;
; The engine's own libraries and nothing else. The platform is named beside the
; layer because a demo of Room or Renderer says so directly; and a demo that
; binds a key names a Camlcast_core.Key rather than a scancode, so nothing here
; reaches past the engine to SDL.

; The public name is the package name, so this installs as lib/camlcast-demo/
; and camlcast.install carries none of it. The hyphen is what does that: a
; public name's first dotted component names the package the stanza belongs to,
; so camlcast.demo would make this a findlib subpackage of the engine and put
; every .ml in this directory into camlcast's own install file — the content
; shipped with the engine, and the camlcast-demo package without its demos.
;
; The executable in bin/ has this same public name and does not collide with it:
; one is a binary in bin/, the other a findlib package in lib/. The module name
; is untouched — it comes from (name) — so every `open Camlcast_demo` and every
; (libraries camlcast_demo) still reads the same.

; Preprocessed, so every world here carries the source position it was written
; at and the dev overlay can find the line behind a wall the player is looking
; at. The studio demo is the one that turns the overlay on, but the rewriter is
; a property of the directory rather than of one file -- dune's check context is
; per directory, and a stanza of its own for one demo would put that demo
; outside the library the catalogue names it from. Every demo being editable is
; the better end of that trade anyway.
;
; The rewriter emits nothing under --profile release; see the (env) stanza in
; the root dune for why a shipped binary carries no source path.

(library
 (name camlcast_demo)
 (public_name camlcast-demo)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_camlcast))
 (libraries camlcast_core camlcast camlcast_edit))
